WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.340
- [Narrator] In most of the world,

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:05.143
horseracing is a fast-paced,
head-spinning event.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.050
But here on Japan's
northernmost island, Hokkaido,

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.686
the races move ...

00:00:10.686 --> 00:00:13.430
(quirky music)

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.430
A little bit slower.

00:00:15.672 --> 00:00:18.255
(quirky music)

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.110
Ban'ei is a form of horseracing
found only in Hokkaido

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.350
in which draft horses pull heavy sleds

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.263
down a 200 meter dirt track.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.300
The sleds can range from
900 to 2,000 pounds,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.580
so Ban'ei horses are often twice as big

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.030
as their speedy counterparts.

00:00:37.014 --> 00:00:38.710
(quirky music)

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.020
Kikuchi Kazuki has been a Ban'ei jockey

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.890
for the past nine years.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.623
But the history of this
race goes back much further.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.460
- [Narrator] The popularity
of the races grew,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.220
and starting in the 1950s
there were four cities

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.680
hosting races across Hokkaido.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.510
However, in recent years
interest has waned.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.370
And today the races are
only held at this racetrack.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.963
But that didn't stop Kikuchi.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.480
- [Narrator] Pulling one-ton
sleds is no easy task.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.490
But these draft horses
race only every two weeks.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.853
And in-between, they're
well taken care of.

00:02:02.348 --> 00:02:03.610
- [Narrator] And for
first time spectators,

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.213
seeing Ban'ei horses
can be a bit of a shock.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.975
- [Narrator] There have been
signs that Ban'ei racing

00:02:20.975 --> 00:02:22.360
may be regaining popularity.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.703
Either way, Kakuchi is happy
to be part of this tradition.

